;;;405     *                      of whether I2C is operating in slave or master mode.
;;;406     *                    - I2C_INT_ACTIVITY: This bit captures I2C activity and stays set until it is cleared.
;;;407     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_DONE: When the I2C is acting as a slave-transmitter, this bit is set to 1 if the
;;;408     *                      master does not acknowledge a transmitted byte. This occurs on the last byte of the
;;;409     *                      transmission, indicating that the transmission is done.
;;;410     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_ABRT: This bit indicates if I2C as an I2C transmitter, is unable to complete the
;;;411     *                      intended actions on the contents of the transmit FIFO.
;;;412     *                    - I2C_INT_RD_REQ: This bit is set to 1 when acting as a slave and another I2C master is
;;;413     *                      attempting to read data.
;;;414     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_EMPTY: This bit is set to 1 when the transmit buffer is at or below the threshold value.
;;;415     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_OVER: Set during transmit if the transmit buffer is filled to Tx FIFO depth and
;;;416     *                      the processor attempts to issue another I2C command.
;;;417     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_FULL: Set when the receive buffer reaches or goes above the RX_TL threshold in the
