;;;973     * @param[in] I2C_IT  This parameter can be one of the following values, refer to @ref I2C_INTERRUPTS.
;;;974     *                    - I2C_INT_MST_ON_HOLD: When master Tx FIFO is empty and no stop bit command is issued, master will hold the SCL low.
;;;975     *                    - I2C_INT_GEN_CALL: Set only when a general call address is received and it is acknowledged.
;;;976     *                    - I2C_INT_START_DET: Indicates whether a START or RESTART condition has occurred on the I2C
;;;977     *                         interface regardless of whether I2C is operating in slave or master mode.
;;;978     *                    - I2C_INT_STOP_DET: Indicates whether a STOP condition has occurred on the I2C interface regardless
;;;979     *                         of whether I2C is operating in slave or master mode.
;;;980     *                    - I2C_INT_ACTIVITY: This bit captures I2C activity and stays set until it is cleared.
;;;981     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_DONE: When the I2C is acting as a slave-transmitter, this bit is set to 1 if the
;;;982     *                         master does not acknowledge a transmitted byte. This occurs on the last byte of
;;;983     *                         the transmission, indicating that the transmission is done.
;;;984     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_ABRT: This bit indicates if I2C, as an I2C transmitter, is unable to complete the
;;;985     *                         intended actions on the contents of the transmit FIFO.
;;;986     *                    - I2C_INT_RD_REQ: This bit is set to 1 when acting as a slave and another I2C master
;;;987     *                         is attempting to read data.
;;;988     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_EMPTY: This bit is set to 1 when the transmit buffer is at or below the threshold value.
;;;989     *                    - I2C_INT_TX_OVER: Set during transmit if the transmit buffer is filled to Tx FIFO depth and
;;;990     *                         the processor attempts to issue another I2C command.
;;;991     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_FULL: Set when the receive buffer reaches or goes above the RX_TL threshold in the
;;;992     *                         IC_RX_TL register.
;;;993     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_OVER: Set if the receive buffer is completely filled to Rx FIFO depth and an
;;;994     *                         additional byte is received from an external I2C device.
;;;995     *                    - I2C_INT_RX_UNDER: Set if the processor attempts to read the receive buffer when it is empty by reading.
;;;996     *
;;;997     * @return The status of I2C interrupt (SET or RESET).
;;;998     * @retval SET    The specified I2C interrupt is set.
;;;999     * @retval RESET  The specified I2C interrupt is reset.
;;;1000    */
