;;;112     *   - the Pin Name column IS the RTL port name (sheet "NOTE", row 20), and the DCI
;;;113     *     signals appear there as dcmi_d[13:0], dcmi_pixclk, dcmi_hsync, dcmi_vsync.
;;;114     *     Note the pin table routes 14 data lines while the IP only has ten: the spec is
;;;115     *     explicit ("DCI 拥有 10 条数据线 D[9:0]", EDM is EDM[0] alone, and unused inputs
;;;116     *     "必须将外部未使用的输入引脚接地"). So d[13:10] are spare board routing, not
;;;117     *     usable DCI data - the 8/10-bit enumeration in this driver is correct;
;;;118     *   - those names form their own class. The same sheet's other pins are either
;;;119     *     P_GPIOx_y (39 of them - SoC GPIOs, the ones a pin mux would apply to) or
;;;120     *     FPGA_IO_PIN_AP/BT/WIFI[n] (42 - reassignable FPGA IO). None of the dcmi_* names
;;;121     *     is a GPIO pin;
;;;122     *   - dcmi_pixclk (FPGA BB9, J4 G5) is on a clock-capable pin, marked *P_*_GC_*, which
