;;;7      /*
;;;8       * DCI demo: framebuffer pool.
;;;9       *
;;;10      * A fixed arena carved into 1 or 2 buffers at run time, rather than a static array
;;;11      * per signal row: the demo has to serve rows from 37 KB to 938 KB and only one runs at
;;;12      * a time, so one arena sized to the budget is both smaller and simpler than a union
;;;13      * of worst cases.
;;;14      *
;;;15      * Every buffer is fenced with guard words. That is the cheapest way to catch a
;;;16      * descriptor whose DAR or BLOCK_TS was computed wrong, and a wrong block split shows
;;;17      * up as an out-of-bounds write before it shows up as a wrong image.
;;;18      */
