;;;499     * measures the uncropped line, and DCI_CropCmd() then re-runs the same arithmetic on the
;;;500     * window - so a row can be refused at Init and never reach the crop at all. The window
;;;501     * always divides in practice, since DCI_ConfigCrop() aligns its width down to 4 pclk, but
;;;502     * that is a property of the driver rather than of this table, so it is checked rather
;;;503     * than assumed.
;;;504     *
;;;505     * 466-raw8 is the row this exists for: 466 bytes per line is even but not a multiple of
;;;506     * 4, so 1-of-2 is legal there and 1-of-4 and 2-of-4 are not.
;;;507     */
